id: pm-web-jpa6
title: GET graph installs or activates pm-graph and bypasses edit permission
description: "GET /api/projects/:projectId/pm/graph calls pmGraphExtensionGraphForProject, which calls ensureGraphExtension. The helper can install npm:pm-graph and activate it, so a safe-method request mutates project state. The pm router's permission middleware exempts GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, which also lets view-only collaborators trigger the mutation. This was found while tracing the complete CSRF boundary for pm-web-413z and must be repaired as a distinct route-semantics/authorization change."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[4]: authorization,http-semantics,pm-graph,security
created_at: "2026-08-30T20:58:12.273Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-26T16:23:29.257Z"
assignee: codex
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "GET /pm/graph is observational and never installs, activates, or otherwise mutates an extension; any explicit provisioning uses a CSRF-protected unsafe method and requires edit permission; view-only users can read the fallback graph without changing project state; real route tests prove command logs remain mutation-free on GET."
why_now: A state-changing GET can be triggered cross-origin and currently bypasses the edit-permission middleware by design.
reviewer: security-review
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-web 2026.8.29 at 7e09ca9
repro_steps: "Request GET /api/projects/:projectId/pm/graph for a project without active pm-graph; pmGraphExtensionGraphForProject calls ensureGraphExtension, which runs pm install and extension activate."
expected_result: GET reads the installed graph when available or returns the fallback graph without mutation.
actual_result: "GET may install and activate pm-graph, including for view-only users."
affected_version: 2026.8.29
component: Graph HTTP routes
customer_impact: Cross-origin or view-only callers can change a project's extension state through a nominally read-only endpoint.
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T15:46:37.359Z",codex,"2026-09-26: GET and HEAD graph read reached extension provisioning under view-only access. Regression test reproduced pm-graph installation before patch. Independent review also found pm extension --json runs installed activate hooks; read path now uses SDK listAllComplete with noExtensions and the built-in graph. Upstream CLI static-inventory request: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1316. Explicit POST graph sync and project creation retain provisioning."
  "2026-09-26T15:49:25.706Z",codex,"2026-09-26 verification: real Postgres + HTTP + PM workspace test failed before the patch because viewer GET installed pm-graph; after the patch it passes for viewer GET/HEAD, owner GET, denied viewer POST, and a missing CLI binary. A local activation-marker extension proves the extension inventory probe executes activate(), while graph GET/HEAD does not. pm test linked acceptance passed (1/1). npm run release:check passed, including npm and Bun packed acceptance. Coverage from coverage/lcov.info: 9,239/10,998 lines (84.01%), 1,344/1,670 branches (80.48%), 395/513 functions (77.00%); 100% target remains open under pm-web-ulgy/pm-web-9ulj. GET now always returns the certified built-in graph; edit-protected POST sync retains pm-graph provisioning."
  "2026-09-26T15:50:25.679Z",codex,"Package fix proposed in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/161 at first head 4640bfe. Review, merge, hosted deployment, and live validation remain pending; this PM issue stays in progress until those independent gates are complete."
  "2026-09-26T16:11:30.506Z",codex,"CodeRabbit exact-head review on 7221dab identified quadratic relationship deduplication after making fallback graph unconditional. Replaced final filter/findIndex with insertion-time Set keys and item-target linear scans with a precomputed item-ID Set; preserved first edge properties. The real HTTP/PostgreSQL/PM regression now creates a blocked-by relation represented in both item fields and dependencies and asserts one BLOCKED_BY edge. Focused test and linked pm test 1/1 passed; full npm run release:check passed. Extension-generated graph compatibility and separate neighbors GET activation remain open follow-up boundaries, not claimed by this route fix."
  "2026-09-26T16:23:29.257Z",codex,Security regression and full release gate re-ran successfully with package runtime SDK @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.26; associated toolchain PM item pm-web-8pml records the exact dependency and packed npm/Bun evidence. The security fix remains unmerged and not hosted.
